<Behavior #eidolon-workflow-architecture-boundaries apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" version="1" (
  <Requirements [
    <Requirement #explicit-architecture-boundaries (
      <Statement ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVR>
      Eidolon workflow integration SHALL use canonical XNL/depa-flows resources, injected Eidolon roots, actor/session effect authority and native surfaces; it SHALL NOT introduce XML authoring, MCP, external agent CLI or parallel flow/runtime authority.
      </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVR>
      <Suites [
        <Suite #resource-and-runtime-authority { name = "Resource and runtime authority" } (
          <Cases [
            <Case #canonical-xnl-and-depa-runtime [
              <Then ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVS>
              it SHALL use canonical depa-flows XNL loaders and Ctrl/Data runtimes
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVS>
              <Then ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVT>
              it SHALL NOT parse XML or implement a parallel scheduler
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVT>
            ] (
              <Given ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVV>
              Ctrl or Data workflow production source
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVV>
              <When ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVW>
              it loads or executes a definition
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVW>
            )>
            <Case #eidolon-roots [
              <Then ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVX>
              injected Eidolon roots SHALL be shared and default ownership SHALL use `.eidolon/workflows`
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVX>
              <Then ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVY>
              workflow resources SHALL remain under the injected Eidolon-owned root
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVY>
            ] (
              <Given ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVZ>
              CLI or TUI constructs the workflow component
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSVZ>
              <When ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW0>
              workspace/global roots are resolved
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW0>
            )>
          ]>
        )>
        <Suite #effect-and-surface-authority { name = "Effect and surface authority" } (
          <Cases [
            <Case #eidolon-effect-lifecycle (
              <Given ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW1>
              a workflow node invokes agent, tool, human or Material work
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW1>
              <When ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW2>
              the effect starts, completes or fails
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW2>
              <Then ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW3>
              Eidolon actor/session/runtime-control SHALL retain lifecycle authority and workflow facts SHALL only reference it
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW3>
            )>
            <Case #native-no-mcp-surface (
              <Given ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW4>
              conversation, TUI or CLI uses workflow capability
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW4>
              <When ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW5>
              it reads or mutates authoring/run facts
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW5>
              <Then ?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW6>
              it SHALL call native component services without MCP, external agent CLI or private mutation paths
              </?01M05F1P2B5D1GR15C8FQFJSW6>
            )>
          ]>
        )>
      ]>
    )>
  ]>
)>
